repository-code: "https://github.com/grahamhaug/Hetarynes_Pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/grahamhaug/Hetarynes_Pipeline"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-15"

abstract: >
  An end-to-end Jupyter Notebook pipeline for curating the HAL-8000
  computational dataset of heterocyclic arynes (hetarynes), comprising
  ~7,143 heterocyclic arenes, ~8,116 derived heterocyclic arynes,
  their DFT-optimized 3D structures (Orca 5.0.3, M06-2X-D3 / def2-SVP),
  calculated dehydrogenation energies, and extracted molecular
  descriptors. Supports data-driven statistical analyses and machine
  learning of hetaryne chemical space.

keywords:
  - hetarynes
  - arynes
  - heteroaromatic
  - DFT
  - density-functional-theory
  - molecular-descriptors
  - cheminformatics
  - SMILES
  - SMARTS
  - rdkit
  - computational-chemistry
  - machine-learning
  - random-forest
  - Morgan-fingerprints

